# i18n translations (en / ru only)

When adding or updating user-facing copy (`$t` / `t` keys):

- **dv-admin** — edit only `apps/dv-admin/src/utils/libs/i18n/locales/en.json` and `ru.json`.
- **pay / pay-simple** — edit only `pay-shared/utils/libs/i18n/locales/en.json` and `ru.json` (shared locales).
- Do **not** create, update, or translate other locale JSON files (`de.json`, `fr.json`, etc.).
- Do **not** restore deleted locale files unless explicitly asked.

Other languages are filled later by the project translator (`yarn i18n` / `@dv.net/translator`) before production.

## Message keys

Use the **English UI string as the key** only when **both** are true:

1. The key itself has **no** line breaks (`\n`)
2. The text is **at most 15 words**

If **either** fails (needs `\n` in the key, **or** more than 15 words) → use a **short abstract key** by meaning (e.g. `API key tooltip`, `PRO tariff description`). Full English copy goes only in the value (the value may still contain `\n` for layout).

```json
// ✅ GOOD — short, no \n in key → key = English
"Shop is accepting payments": "Shop is accepting payments"

// ✅ GOOD — short English key; \n only in value for layout
"Add your IP address to the whitelist": "Add your IP address\nto the whitelist"
"Just set up the API and start accepting payments right away": "Just set up the API\nand start accepting payments right away"

// ✅ GOOD — long text → short abstract key
"API key tooltip": "Authenticates API requests for invoices, payments, and shop operations. Keep it private and regenerate it if it may have been exposed"
"PRO tariff description": "This is a version of our Open Source\nMerchant on our servers"

// ❌ BAD — long English used as key
"Authenticates API requests for invoices, payments, and shop operations. Keep it private and regenerate it if it may have been exposed": "…"
```

## Trailing punctuation

In **keys and values**, do **not** put trailing punctuation (`:`, `.`, `!`, `?`, …). Add punctuation in the template/code when needed. A trailing period is **never** needed.

```json
// ❌ BAD
"Payments:": "Платежи:",
"Webhook status.": "Статус вебхука.",
"In progress!": "В процессе!"

// ✅ GOOD
"Payments": "Платежи",
"Webhook status": "Статус вебхука",
"In progress": "В процессе"
```

```vue
{{ $t('Payments') }}:
```
